{"type":"message","id":"2dd9eee6","parentId":"ecc32fb2","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:28:48.806Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_3a5lp2uwda85_1","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"site:github.com openclaw skill security scanner malware detection 2026\",\n  \"provider\": \"miaoda\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"OpenClaw Skill Scanner\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/YutianGe/openclaw-skill-scanner/blob/main/README_EN.md\",\n      \"description\": \"YutianGe\\nd32efca · Mar 12, 2026\\n447 lines (338 loc) · 15.6 KB\\n...\\nIt intelligently detects potential security risks including dangerous commands, sensitive file access, external requests, prompt injection, and more. Through heuristic detection and optional Ollama local LLM enhancement, it can automatically discover unknown malicious patterns without manual rule maintenance.\\n✨ Key Features\\n🔍 Smart Scanning Engine\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"[Feature]: Add skill/extension security scanning pipeline to detect malicious skills before execution #11014\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/11014\",\n      \"description\": \"Binary file detection - Flag any binary executables included in skill packages\\nPhase 2: Behavioral Analysis (Medium Cost, High Impact)\\nAdd AST-based dataflow analysis for skill code:\\nTaint tracking - Track data flow from sensitive sources (credential files, environment variables, function parameters) to dangerous sinks (network calls, eval/exec, subprocess)\\nCross-file analysis - Detect exfiltration chains split across multiple files (collector.py -> encoder.py -> reporter.py)\\nControl...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"🛡️ Ronald Skill Auditor\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/Gotbuds/skill-auditor\",\n      \"description\": \"Gotbuds/skill-auditor\\nCode\\n<table>\\n<tr><td>Gotbuds</td></tr>\\n<tr><td>checks</td><td>checks</td><td>Initial commit - Ronald Skill Auditor v1.0</td><td></td></tr>\\n<tr><td>reports</td><td>reports</td><td>Initial commit - Ronald Skill Auditor v1.0</td><td></td></tr>\\n<tr...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"explain-openclaw/08-security-analysis/ecosystem-security-threats.md at master · centminmod/explain-openclaw · GitHub\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/centminmod/explain-openclaw/blob/master/08-security-analysis/ecosystem-security-threats.md\",\n      \"description\": \"305 lines (237 loc) · 23 KB\\nEcosystem Security Threats\\nThese are not codebase vulnerabilities. The threats below target OpenClaw users through supply chain attacks, social engineering, and infrastructure misconfiguration. They apply to any popular self-hosted AI framework, not just OpenClaw.\\nThis section was prompted by a community security advisory from @edgeaiplanet on Threads.\\nContents\\nOfficial packages and accounts\\n1. npm Typosqu...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"ClawHub Scanner 🕵️‍♂️\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/move78ai/clawhub-malware-scanner\",\n      \"description\": \"ClawHub Scanner helps developers and enterprises verify their agent environments against known Indicators of Compromise (IOCs) and high-risk permission patterns.\\n⚡ Features\\nIOC Scanning: Checks for known malicious C2 IP addresses (e.g., 91.92.xx.xx) and domain signatures.\\nPayload Detection: Scans for known malware filenames (e.g., openclaw-agent.zip, atomic_stealer).\\nObfuscation Detection: Flags...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Proposal: Security Gateway Framework for Third-Party Skill Installation #9256\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/9256\",\n      \"description\": \"Supply chain attacks\\nSensitive data theft\\nBackdoor programs\\n...\\nSemgrep / CodeQL - Code pattern scanning\\nSnyk / npm audit - Vulnerability detection\\nOSQuery - Runtime behavior monitoring\\nVirusTotal API - Malware detection\\n👤 User Experience\\nPre-Installation Warning\\n<beginning of the code>\\n⚠️ Security Warning: [Skill Name]\\n\\nRisk Level: 🟡 MEDIUM\\n\\nDetected:\\n• Requests exec tool access\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"GitHub - gavin2us/clawshield: Security scanner for OpenClaw skills - detect malicious patterns, data exfiltration, and supply chain risks · GitHub\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/gavin2us/clawshield\",\n      \"description\": \"Why ClawShield?\\nOpenClaw skills can execute code, access files, make network requests, and read secrets. A malicious skill can:\\n🔑 Steal API keys and credentials\\n📤 Exfiltrate sensitive data\\n💰 Hijack crypto wallets\\n🚪 Install backdoors and persistence mechanisms\\n⛏️ Run cryptominers\\nClawShield catches these threats before you install.\\nClawShield includes 30+ detection rules across categories:\\n...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"ClawSecure — OpenClaw Security Scanner & Audit Platform\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/ClawSecure/clawsecure-openclaw-security\",\n      \"description\": \"ClawSecure is the independent integrity layer for the OpenClaw ecosystem — a free OpenClaw security scanner and audit platform purpose-built for AI agent skills and workflows. Layer 1 — Proprietary Threat Intelligence ClawSecure's proprietary engine analyzes skills against 55+ OpenClaw-specific threat patterns, including ClawHavoc detection, ReDoS vulnerabilities, and Context-Aware Intelligence that differentiates real threats from normal agent capabilities.\\nLayer 2 — Advanced Static &...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Security: More social engineering malware in skills — integrate automated security scanning in publish pipeline #91\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/clawhub/issues/91\",\n      \"description\": \"Urgency pattern detection — flag repeated \\\"must install\\\", \\\"will not work without\\\", \\\"IMPORTANT\\\" pressure tactics\\nAuthor reputation — new accounts publishing skills that reference external executables should get extra scrutiny\\nWe're happy to contribute our YARA ruleset as a starting point. The rules catch both this skill and the previous <beginning of the code>JordanPrater<end of the code> batch with zero false positives on legitimate skills.\\nEvidence\\nGitHub repo (payload host...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Feature Proposal: Security Scan Hook API for skill:install #18677\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/18677\",\n      \"description\": \"Feature Proposal: Security Scan Hook API for skill:install #18677\\nLabels\\nsecurity\\nstale\\nkoatora20\\nSummary\\nWhen users install skills from ClawHub or external sources, there is currently no hook point to run security scanning before the skill becomes active. This proposal suggests adding a <beginning of the code>skill:before_install<end of the code> hook event that security tools can intercept.\\nMotivation\\nOpenClaw's Virus...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"site:github.com openclaw skill security scanner malware detection 2026","provider":"miaoda","count":10,"results":[{"title":"OpenClaw Skill Scanner","url":"https://github.com/YutianGe/openclaw-skill-scanner/blob/main/README_EN.md","description":"YutianGe\nd32efca · Mar 12, 2026\n447 lines (338 loc) · 15.6 KB\n...\nIt intelligently detects potential security risks including dangerous commands, sensitive file access, external requests, prompt injection, and more. Through heuristic detection and optional Ollama local LLM enhancement, it can automatically discover unknown malicious patterns without manual rule maintenance.\n✨ Key Features\n🔍 Smart Scanning Engine\n","siteName":""},{"title":"[Feature]: Add skill/extension security scanning pipeline to detect malicious skills before execution #11014","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/11014","description":"Binary file detection - Flag any binary executables included in skill packages\nPhase 2: Behavioral Analysis (Medium Cost, High Impact)\nAdd AST-based dataflow analysis for skill code:\nTaint tracking - Track data flow from sensitive sources (credential files, environment variables, function parameters) to dangerous sinks (network calls, eval/exec, subprocess)\nCross-file analysis - Detect exfiltration chains split across multiple files (collector.py -> encoder.py -> reporter.py)\nControl...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"🛡️ Ronald Skill Auditor","url":"https://github.com/Gotbuds/skill-auditor","description":"Gotbuds/skill-auditor\nCode\n<table>\n<tr><td>Gotbuds</td></tr>\n<tr><td>checks</td><td>checks</td><td>Initial commit - Ronald Skill Auditor v1.0</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>reports</td><td>reports</td><td>Initial commit - Ronald Skill Auditor v1.0</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"explain-openclaw/08-security-analysis/ecosystem-security-threats.md at master · centminmod/explain-openclaw · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/centminmod/explain-openclaw/blob/master/08-security-analysis/ecosystem-security-threats.md","description":"305 lines (237 loc) · 23 KB\nEcosystem Security Threats\nThese are not codebase vulnerabilities. The threats below target OpenClaw users through supply chain attacks, social engineering, and infrastructure misconfiguration. They apply to any popular self-hosted AI framework, not just OpenClaw.\nThis section was prompted by a community security advisory from @edgeaiplanet on Threads.\nContents\nOfficial packages and accounts\n1. npm Typosqu...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"ClawHub Scanner 🕵️‍♂️","url":"https://github.com/move78ai/clawhub-malware-scanner","description":"ClawHub Scanner helps developers and enterprises verify their agent environments against known Indicators of Compromise (IOCs) and high-risk permission patterns.\n⚡ Features\nIOC Scanning: Checks for known malicious C2 IP addresses (e.g., 91.92.xx.xx) and domain signatures.\nPayload Detection: Scans for known malware filenames (e.g., openclaw-agent.zip, atomic_stealer).\nObfuscation Detection: Flags...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"Proposal: Security Gateway Framework for Third-Party Skill Installation #9256","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/9256","description":"Supply chain attacks\nSensitive data theft\nBackdoor programs\n...\nSemgrep / CodeQL - Code pattern scanning\nSnyk / npm audit - Vulnerability detection\nOSQuery - Runtime behavior monitoring\nVirusTotal API - Malware detection\n👤 User Experience\nPre-Installation Warning\n<beginning of the code>\n⚠️ Security Warning: [Skill Name]\n\nRisk Level: 🟡 MEDIUM\n\nDetected:\n• Requests exec tool access\n","siteName":""},{"title":"GitHub - gavin2us/clawshield: Security scanner for OpenClaw skills - detect malicious patterns, data exfiltration, and supply chain risks · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/gavin2us/clawshield","description":"Why ClawShield?\nOpenClaw skills can execute code, access files, make network requests, and read secrets. A malicious skill can:\n🔑 Steal API keys and credentials\n📤 Exfiltrate sensitive data\n💰 Hijack crypto wallets\n🚪 Install backdoors and persistence mechanisms\n⛏️ Run cryptominers\nClawShield catches these threats before you install.\nClawShield includes 30+ detection rules across categories:\n...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"ClawSecure — OpenClaw Security Scanner & Audit Platform","url":"https://github.com/ClawSecure/clawsecure-openclaw-security","description":"ClawSecure is the independent integrity layer for the OpenClaw ecosystem — a free OpenClaw security scanner and audit platform purpose-built for AI agent skills and workflows. Layer 1 — Proprietary Threat Intelligence ClawSecure's proprietary engine analyzes skills against 55+ OpenClaw-specific threat patterns, including ClawHavoc detection, ReDoS vulnerabilities, and Context-Aware Intelligence that differentiates real threats from normal agent capabilities.\nLayer 2 — Advanced Static &...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"Security: More social engineering malware in skills — integrate automated security scanning in publish pipeline #91","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/clawhub/issues/91","description":"Urgency pattern detection — flag repeated \"must install\", \"will not work without\", \"IMPORTANT\" pressure tactics\nAuthor reputation — new accounts publishing skills that reference external executables should get extra scrutiny\nWe're happy to contribute our YARA ruleset as a starting point. The rules catch both this skill and the previous <beginning of the code>JordanPrater<end of the code> batch with zero false positives on legitimate skills.\nEvidence\nGitHub repo (payload host...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"Feature Proposal: Security Scan Hook API for skill:install #18677","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/18677","description":"Feature Proposal: Security Scan Hook API for skill:install #18677\nLabels\nsecurity\nstale\nkoatora20\nSummary\nWhen users install skills from ClawHub or external sources, there is currently no hook point to run security scanning before the skill becomes active. This proposal suggests adding a <beginning of the code>skill:before_install<end of the code> hook event that security tools can intercept.\nMotivation\nOpenClaw's Virus...\n","siteName":""}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1776331728806}}
{"type":"message","id":"bae3eefa","parentId":"2dd9eee6","timestamp":"2026-04-16T09:28:48.996Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_3a5lp2uwda85_2","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"github.com clawhub skill security audit open source\",\n  \"provider\": \"miaoda\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"ClawHub:OpenClaw生态的“应用商店“，如何让AI助手真正“动起来“-CSDN博客\",\n      \"url\": \"https://blog.csdn.net/weixin_45110225/article/details/157764790\",\n      \"description\": \"但在你兴奋地准备安装各种神奇技能之前，我们需要先理解一个关键问题：这个开放生态既带来了无限可能，也引入了新的安全风险。2026年2月的安全审计显示，ClawHub上2857个技能中，有341个恶意技能（约12%）正在窃取用户数据。\\n本文将带你深入理解ClawHub的技术定位、核心功能、使用方式，并提供安全...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"OpenClaw Security\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/guard0-ai/g0/blob/main/docs/openclaw-security.md\",\n      \"description\": \"Code\\n724 lines (559 loc) · 33.8 KB\\nOpenClaw Security\\ng0 provides the most comprehensive security coverage for OpenClaw — one of the most...\\nOpenClaw (formerly Clawdbot / Moltbot) is an autonomous AI agent framework that connects any LLM to everyday messaging apps — WhatsApp, Telegram, Slack — and autonomously executes tasks: sending emails, calling APIs, browsing the web, and running scheduled jobs. \",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"GitHub - claude-go/clawhub-bridge: Security scanner for AI agent skills — 57 patterns, 13 categories, capability lattice. Zero dependencies. · GitHub\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/claude-go/clawhub-bridge\",\n      \"description\": \"Security scanner for AI agent skills and MCP servers. Detects malicious patterns, infers capability requirements, and blocks dangerous skills before they reach your system.\\nCovers 7 of 10 OWASP MCP Top 10 risks through static analysis. Built because 12% of a real AI agent marketplace was malicious.\\nInstall\\nIt scans skill content for 104 malicious patterns across 29 categories, infers a capability profile (what the skill actually needs access...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Claw Security Scanner\",\n      \"url\": \"https://clawhub.ai/BetsyMalthus/claw-security-scanner\",\n      \"description\": \"Claw Security Scanner\\n自动扫描OpenClaw技能文件，检测恶意代码、凭据泄露、依赖漏洞及权限风险，提供安全评估与修复建议。\\nMIT-0 · Free to use, modify, and redistribute. No attribution required.\\nby\\nopenclaw/skills tree or enable automatic fixes — treat it as a powerful tool that can read many files and modify them. Enabling networked reporting/notifications or the Docker image without vetting could allow exfiltration of findings...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"ClawSecure — OpenClaw Security Scanner & Audit Platform\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/ClawSecure/clawsecure-openclaw-security\",\n      \"description\": \"ClawSecure is the independent integrity layer for the OpenClaw ecosystem — a free OpenClaw security scanner and audit platform purpose-built for AI agent skills and workflows. <tr><td>OWASP ASI Top 10 Scanner</td><td>Comprehensive OpenClaw security coverage across all 10 agentic security categories defined by the OWASP Agentic Security Initiative — from agent goal hijack and tool misuse to data exfiltration and agent persistence</td></tr>...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"GitHub - torkjacobs/tork-scan: Security scanner for ClawHub skills — detect malicious patterns in AI agent tools · GitHub\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/torkjacobs/tork-scan\",\n      \"description\": \"Detect malicious patterns in AI agent tools before they compromise your system. No Tork account required.\\nLike <beginning of the code>npm audit<end...\\nTork provides independent AI agent governance — like SSL certificates for AI. This scanner is free and open-source. No account required.\\nFor real-time governance, trust badges, and compliance receipts, visit tork.network.\\nLicense\\nMIT - see LICENSE\\nTypeScript 91.0%\\nJavaScript 9.0%\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Agent Audit Scanner\",\n      \"url\": \"https://clawhub.ai/HeadyZhang/agent-audit-scanner\",\n      \"description\": \"Heady · @HeadyZhang\\nMIT-0\\nSecurity Scan\\nVirusTotal\\nBenign\\nOpenClaw\\nOpenClaw\\nBenign\\nhigh confidence\\nThe skill is a coherent auditing wrapper that reads OpenClaw skill directories and config and runs an external 'agent-audit' scanner; its requirements and instructions align with that purpose.\\nDetails\\nPurpose & Capability\\nName/description (security scanner for OpenClaw skills) aligns with required binaries (python3...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Researchers Find 341 Malicious ClawHub Skills Stealing Data from OpenClaw Users\",\n      \"url\": \"https://buaq.net/go-392476.html\",\n      \"description\": \" 文章主要讲的是Koi Security在ClawHub平台上发现的恶意技能。ClawHub是一个允许用户安装第三方技能的市场，但安全审计发现有341个恶意技能，涉及多个活动。这些恶意技能伪装成各种工具，比如加密货币钱包、YouTube工具等，诱导用户执行恶意命令，窃取敏感信息。ClawHub is a marketplace designed to make it easy for OpenClaw users to find and install third-party skills. It...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"OpenClaw AI Assistant: Record GitHub Growth, Record Security Crisis\",\n      \"url\": \"https://byteiota.com/openclaw-ai-assistant-record-github-growth-record-security-crisis/\",\n      \"description\": \"Within weeks, SecurityScorecard discovered 40,214 exposed OpenClaw instances —63% vulnerable to remote code execution attacks. The culprit: developers deployed OpenClaw with default settings that bind to 0.0.0.0:3000 (publicly exposed) with no authentication. CVE-2026-25253 (CVSS 8.8) allowed attackers to compromise systems through a single malicious webpage. 1...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"GitHub - prompt-security/clawsec: A complete security skill suite for OpenClaw's and NanoClaw agents (and variants). Protect your SOUL.md (etc') with drift detection, live security recommendations, au\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/prompt-security/clawsec\",\n      \"description\": \"🌐 Live at: https://clawsec.prompt.security https://prompt.security/clawsec\\n🦞 What is ClawSec?\\nClawSec is a complete security skill suite for AI agent platforms. It provides unified security monitoring, integrity verification, and threat intelligence-protecting your agent's cognitive architecture against prompt injection, drift, and malicious instructions.\\nSupported Platforms\\nOpenClaw (MoltBot, Clawdbot, and clones) - Full suite with skill...\\n\",\n      \"siteName\": \"\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"github.com clawhub skill security audit open source","provider":"miaoda","count":10,"results":[{"title":"ClawHub:OpenClaw生态的“应用商店“，如何让AI助手真正“动起来“-CSDN博客","url":"https://blog.csdn.net/weixin_45110225/article/details/157764790","description":"但在你兴奋地准备安装各种神奇技能之前，我们需要先理解一个关键问题：这个开放生态既带来了无限可能，也引入了新的安全风险。2026年2月的安全审计显示，ClawHub上2857个技能中，有341个恶意技能（约12%）正在窃取用户数据。\n本文将带你深入理解ClawHub的技术定位、核心功能、使用方式，并提供安全...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"OpenClaw Security","url":"https://github.com/guard0-ai/g0/blob/main/docs/openclaw-security.md","description":"Code\n724 lines (559 loc) · 33.8 KB\nOpenClaw Security\ng0 provides the most comprehensive security coverage for OpenClaw — one of the most...\nOpenClaw (formerly Clawdbot / Moltbot) is an autonomous AI agent framework that connects any LLM to everyday messaging apps — WhatsApp, Telegram, Slack — and autonomously executes tasks: sending emails, calling APIs, browsing the web, and running scheduled jobs. ","siteName":""},{"title":"GitHub - claude-go/clawhub-bridge: Security scanner for AI agent skills — 57 patterns, 13 categories, capability lattice. Zero dependencies. · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/claude-go/clawhub-bridge","description":"Security scanner for AI agent skills and MCP servers. Detects malicious patterns, infers capability requirements, and blocks dangerous skills before they reach your system.\nCovers 7 of 10 OWASP MCP Top 10 risks through static analysis. Built because 12% of a real AI agent marketplace was malicious.\nInstall\nIt scans skill content for 104 malicious patterns across 29 categories, infers a capability profile (what the skill actually needs access...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"Claw Security Scanner","url":"https://clawhub.ai/BetsyMalthus/claw-security-scanner","description":"Claw Security Scanner\n自动扫描OpenClaw技能文件，检测恶意代码、凭据泄露、依赖漏洞及权限风险，提供安全评估与修复建议。\nMIT-0 · Free to use, modify, and redistribute. No attribution required.\nby\nopenclaw/skills tree or enable automatic fixes — treat it as a powerful tool that can read many files and modify them. Enabling networked reporting/notifications or the Docker image without vetting could allow exfiltration of findings...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"ClawSecure — OpenClaw Security Scanner & Audit Platform","url":"https://github.com/ClawSecure/clawsecure-openclaw-security","description":"ClawSecure is the independent integrity layer for the OpenClaw ecosystem — a free OpenClaw security scanner and audit platform purpose-built for AI agent skills and workflows. <tr><td>OWASP ASI Top 10 Scanner</td><td>Comprehensive OpenClaw security coverage across all 10 agentic security categories defined by the OWASP Agentic Security Initiative — from agent goal hijack and tool misuse to data exfiltration and agent persistence</td></tr>...\n","siteName":""},{"title":"GitHub - torkjacobs/tork-scan: Security scanner for ClawHub skills — detect malicious patterns in AI agent tools · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/torkjacobs/tork-scan","description":"Detect malicious patterns in AI agent tools before they compromise your system. No Tork account required.\nLike <beginning of the code>npm audit<end...\nTork provides independent AI agent governance — like SSL certificates for AI. This scanner is free and open-source. No account required.\nFor