{"type":"message","id":"80a830d4","parentId":"0e25344c","timestamp":"2026-04-16T22:29:35.910Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_nv65x4563ybq_1","toolName":"sessions_history","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"sessionKey\": \"agent:main:feishu:direct:ou_fc1e75d64fec6e10ce94a51adc6f6409\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"Let me check the arc-skill-scanner SKILL.md to understand how to use it, and also look for scanning scripts.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_function_z6tx29udqn31_1\",\n          \"name\": \"exec\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"command\": \"cat ~/workspace/agent/workspace/skills/arc-skill-scanner/SKILL.md 2>/dev/null | head -60\",\n            \"timeout\": 10\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_function_z6tx29udqn31_2\",\n          \"name\": \"exec\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"command\": \"ls -la ~/workspace/agent/workspace/skills/arc-skill-scanner/scripts/ 2>/dev/null\",\n            \"timeout\": 10\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n      \"provider\": \"minimax-token-plan\",\n      \"model\": \"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1776334547220,\n      \"responseId\": \"062fe9d3907800943e17f3f86951a2a3\",\n      \"__openclaw\": {\n        \"id\": \"fedfca82\",\n        \"seq\": 669\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"I found that arc-skill-scanner has a scanner.py script. Let me run it to scan all installed skills. I should use the scan-all command or scan each skill directory.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_function_ft0q3h1akkbc_1\",\n          \"name\": \"exec\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"command\": \"cd ~/workspace/agent/workspace && python3 ~/workspace/agent/workspace/skills/arc-skill-scanner/scripts/scanner.py scan-all 2>&1\",\n            \"timeout\": 120\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n      \"provider\": \"minimax-token-plan\",\n      \"model\": \"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1776334549922,\n      \"responseId\": \"062fe9d612776613dbb0d6d0222000f9\",\n      \"__openclaw\": {\n        \"id\": \"39d02e35\",\n        \"seq\": 672\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"The exec tool is refusing to run with the cd && python3 pattern. Let me try a different approach.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_function_ue26igxttgah_1\",\n          \"name\": \"exec\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"command\": \"python3 /home/gem/workspace/agent/workspace/skills/arc-skill-scanner/scripts/scanner.py scan-all 2>&1\",\n            \"timeout\": 120\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n      \"provider\": \"minimax-token-plan\",\n      \"model\": \"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1776334552775,\n      \"responseId\": \"062fe9d8f1a296277a1094fe1327d452\",\n      \"__openclaw\": {\n        \"id\": \"ed4cd8f8\",\n        \"seq\": 674\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"The scan found 12 issues across 4 skills. But wait - feishu-mcp-bot and mcporter are not in my skills list. Let me check if there's something outside of my workspace skills directory. The scanner scanned \\\"4 installed skills\\\"